Subject: [PATCH 1/6] Allow selection, copy, and link clicks in Docs viewer
 mode

Read-only Docs mode constructed no TextEditor, so viewers could not
select text, copy it, or open hyperlinks even though none of those
mutate the document. Reuse the existing editor machinery instead of
duplicating it: construct the TextEditor in read-only mode too and
thread a readOnly flag that gates every mutating path (typing, IME,
paste, cut, table-border resize, header/footer edit-context switch)
while leaving drag selection, copy serialization, and link opening
intact. A plain click on a link opens it (Google-Docs viewer parity);
a drag still selects. The link popover hides its Edit/Remove buttons
in read-only mode.

Fixes #482

