Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Guard read-only mutations at the EditorAPI boundary

Read-only viewer mode only gated pointer/keyboard/clipboard event
handlers. The programmatic EditorAPI (paste -> TextEditor.pasteContent,
plus applyStyle, insertLink, table/image ops) mutates the store directly
and bypasses those handlers, so any holder of the api object could still
alter a viewer's document (CodeRabbit Major finding).

Neutralize every mutating EditorAPI command at the API boundary via an
allowlist no-op wrapper, and gate the direct TextEditor.pasteContent /
insertText entry points to mirror handlePaste / handleInput. This stays
client-side defense-in-depth; the store/server remains the authoritative
write boundary. Adds non-vacuous programmatic-path tests (applyStyle /
insertLink / insertTable, each with a not-read-only control).

